  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Mix 680 g ground beef (80/20), 30 g panko, 1 egg, 1/2 onion, grated, 1 tbsp shoyu (soy sauce), 3/4 tsp salt and 1/2 tsp black pepper just until combined. Shape into 4 patties about 2 cm thick, with a dimple in the center so they stay flat.",
      "ingredientRefs": [
        0,
        1,
        2,
        3,
        4,
        5,
        6
      ],
      "timers": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat 1 tbsp neutral oil in a large skillet over medium-high and cook the patties 4 minutes per side, until browned and cooked through. Transfer to a plate and pour off all but 1 tbsp fat.",
      "ingredientRefs": [
        7
      ],
      "timers": [
        {
          "text": "4 minutes",
          "seconds": 240
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Add 2 tbsp butter to the pan with 1/2 onion, thinly sliced (for the gravy) and 150 g button mushrooms, sliced. Cook 5 minutes over medium, scraping up the browned bits, until the mushrooms are golden.",
      "ingredientRefs": [
        8,
        9,
        10
      ],
      "timers": [
        {
          "text": "5 minutes",
          "seconds": 300
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Sprinkle in 2 tbsp all-purpose flour and stir 1 minute. Whisk in 480 ml beef stock, 1 tbsp shoyu (for the gravy) and 1 tsp Worcestershire sauce, bring to a simmer and cook 3 minutes, until thick enough to coat a spoon. Return the patties to the gravy to warm through.",
      "ingredientRefs": [
        11,
        12,
        13,
        14
      ],
      "timers": [
        {
          "text": "1 minute",
          "seconds": 60
        },
        {
          "text": "3 minutes",
          "seconds": 180
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In a separate pan, fry 4 eggs sunny side up, about 3 minutes, until the whites are set and the yolks runny.",
      "ingredientRefs": [
        15
      ],
      "timers": [
        {
          "text": "3 minutes",
          "seconds": 180
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Scoop 900 g hot cooked white rice into bowls, top each with a patty, plenty of gravy and an egg. Scatter with 2 scallions, sliced.",
      "ingredientRefs": [
        16,
        17
      ],
      "timers": []
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The gravy is the point: make it in the patty pan so it picks up the fond. Add a splash more stock if it tightens while standing. Shoyu in both the patty and the gravy is the local touch. Some spots add Spam or Portuguese sausage alongside.",
